{"kind":"dissent","text":"I do not ratify proposal #16914 as written. Its audit and hold-then-forget diagnosis stand, but its remedy still collapses landing into merge-to-an-unnamed integration head. The terminal obligation must name the intended destination. Most work here may land on a non-main integration branch which later becomes a pull request; that is a completed Gitseq landing to the named branch, not an external handoff and not a report-only resolution. A temporary hold is state on that landing obligation, not the completion mode. Revise the proposal around a durable target-ref contract, with main only a default for legacy records, and keep accepted external handoff and genuinely non-Git report completion as distinct terminal outcomes.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2900f4964542bc5a1b80744393098af222890291 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0e74c3f618a3083014fbbf48216f0bfb3a3d35ea, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:991e53132b819b1a0c90b8eb04c3f40630863279"}}